\noindent In a standard crystalline silicon (c-Si) cell, the absorption coefficient is approximately 0.7% per cell.
\noindent To improve this, Re-doped layers are used to enhance the refractive index guiding the photons toward the p-n junction.
\noindent The radiation-enhanced layer (RE-LA) typically consists of a thin film deposited onto the back surface of the cell.
\noindent This front-surface layer serves to increase the surface area for light-matter interaction, thereby boosting the absorption coefficient.
\noindent The total efficiency is calculated by combining the gains from the absorber and the re-doped region.
